                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "cfe40dd3-0df0-4e66-9dc1-64bec7c53f16",
                        "entry_id": "654b5ef4-a32d-3604-8ce8-fb062e13bf88",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "зна́харях"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "56896e60-f598-32ef-9294-cdec54f03fa5",
                        "entry_id": "654b5ef4-a32d-3604-8ce8-fb062e13bf88",
                        "glosses": [
                            "тот, кто лечит народными средствами, используя также элементы магии, колдовские приёмы и заговоры, а также методы энергетического воздействия"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c8f354f6-0c98-4e84-a51c-3606ece84153",
                                "sense_id": "56896e60-f598-32ef-9294-cdec54f03fa5",
                                "text": "Жена несколько раз ходила к знахарям и лекаркам, которые ещё не перевелись в Москве, потратила много денег, а толку не было."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a666c2d3-06a3-4f87-ac5b-7682bf6e369e",
                                "sense_id": "56896e60-f598-32ef-9294-cdec54f03fa5",
                                "text": "Есть знахари, что тёмной силой орудуют, и то человеку на вред и погибель…"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cbba9318-1460-4e42-a208-0b01743d54f8",
                                "sense_id": "56896e60-f598-32ef-9294-cdec54f03fa5",
                                "text": "Он лечился, но врачи не помогали, и тогда няня привела знахаря из Петровского посада, который должен был приказать больному пианисту отбросить костыли и начать ходить, как здоровые люди."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f1fbf49c-488e-4fb6-ae2d-7c207af7b098",
                        "source_entry_id": "654b5ef4-a32d-3604-8ce8-fb062e13bf88",
                        "source_sense_id": "56896e60-f598-32ef-9294-cdec54f03fa5",
                        "target_lang_word": "healer",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "healer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "36872cce-0482-3d46-9ee6-7d0e068dd2de",
                                        "entry_id": "e72205dd-531a-3914-8a38-cf49698f05b5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who heals, especially through faith."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d441dcf0-d320-4842-9bc3-ae02d47c500c",
                                                "sense_id": "36872cce-0482-3d46-9ee6-7d0e068dd2de",
                                                "text": "faith healer"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a275a10a-41a9-436a-9876-b8bd859c6906",
                                                "sense_id": "36872cce-0482-3d46-9ee6-7d0e068dd2de",
                                                "text": "gifted healer"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b46eaf56-3c39-4cc3-b7bf-1039fe29d656",
                                                "sense_id": "36872cce-0482-3d46-9ee6-7d0e068dd2de",
                                                "text": "natural healer"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd23acc3-3cf6-49b2-a8db-7cdadb5b38cd",
                                                "sense_id": "36872cce-0482-3d46-9ee6-7d0e068dd2de",
                                                "text": "The villagers sought help from a traditional healer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c75799dc-712d-4161-ad9b-56a7a4c89ab0",
                                                "sense_id": "36872cce-0482-3d46-9ee6-7d0e068dd2de",
                                                "text": "She became known as a spiritual healer."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "013a53aa-5d64-3831-af87-fcef2e95ad46",
                                        "entry_id": "e72205dd-531a-3914-8a38-cf49698f05b5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Anything that heals; a medicine that heals some wound, injury, ailment, or disease."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6ca5ce45-546d-4fc5-b5db-9956d9cc1777",
                        "source_entry_id": "654b5ef4-a32d-3604-8ce8-fb062e13bf88",
                        "source_sense_id": "56896e60-f598-32ef-9294-cdec54f03fa5",
                        "target_lang_word": "medicine man",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "medicine man",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7e3b1f43-73d5-3d7c-a628-4890d6875604",
                                        "entry_id": "2805ec09-9965-3916-a455-05c6880e0e88",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A Native American shamanistic healer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a3e3a12-1d63-4092-851e-662744da7a9f",
                                                "sense_id": "7e3b1f43-73d5-3d7c-a628-4890d6875604",
                                                "text": "And the Jossakeeds, the Prophets,\nThe Wabenos, the Magicians,\nAnd the Medicine-men, the Medas,\nPainted upon bark and deer-skin\nFigures for the songs they chanted"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e7f6cbc-8ee8-4951-8740-f8ccd0ad1b42",
                                                "sense_id": "7e3b1f43-73d5-3d7c-a628-4890d6875604",
                                                "text": "Sitting Bull is commonly thought of as a warrior. In point of fact he was not. He was a “medicine man;” which means that he included within himself the three professions of the priesthood, medicine and law."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "12fc5714-75a2-3725-b3e9-91b271b5103d",
                                        "entry_id": "2805ec09-9965-3916-a455-05c6880e0e88",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A traditional healer among other indigenous or ancient peoples."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "98736e65-66ee-4f5d-8e4d-29790ece7317",
                                                "sense_id": "12fc5714-75a2-3725-b3e9-91b271b5103d",
                                                "text": "When, however, the plant spirits were not strong enough in themselves, then the family called in the Medicine Man. He appeared, a \"monster of so frightful mien\", with noise making apparatus which produced such a terrifying din that even the hardiest demon was likely to flee."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2bd8b268-4485-4fea-b5dc-8d757fa60891",
                                                "sense_id": "12fc5714-75a2-3725-b3e9-91b271b5103d",
                                                "text": "\"I'm sorry kiddies,\" he said, \"but I haven't very much faith in Medicine Men.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0c3486e7-7077-4b38-8a87-4528155e9dbf",
                                                "sense_id": "12fc5714-75a2-3725-b3e9-91b271b5103d",
                                                "text": "After the death of Ekwefi's second child, Okonkwo had gone to a medicine man, who was also a diviner of the Afa Oracle, to enquire what was amiss."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "428e29e2-7fbe-3d3d-9c09-a15bdcebcef5",
                                        "entry_id": "2805ec09-9965-3916-a455-05c6880e0e88",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The pitchman at a medicine show."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "67e6fdae-f284-425e-a7fa-48f53693aaa9",
                                                "sense_id": "428e29e2-7fbe-3d3d-9c09-a15bdcebcef5",
                                                "text": "One of the most successful of the tent road-showmen is Dr. J. Van Cleve, old-time medicine man, who operates out of Portland. Van Cleve pitches his tent for a week and shows a different film program each night combined with a vaude show."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20d7e5d1-150d-4315-b6ff-246b3afcb40b",
                                                "sense_id": "428e29e2-7fbe-3d3d-9c09-a15bdcebcef5",
                                                "text": "the medicine man offered free entertainment in exchange for an opportunity to sell hope to a nation of individually troubled people."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": [
